            <ArticleTitle>Chronic persistent knee pain after repeated diagnostic arthroscopy: osteoid osteoma, a primarily overlooked diagnosis in a young woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of osteoid osteoma of the distal femur in an adolescent female patient that was primarily overlooked and led to repeated diagnostic arthroscopy of the knee. A thorough history and physical examination of the joint as well as adequate roentgenographic studies could have spared this patient two unnecessary arthroscopies and indicated the correct therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
